<title>INDIA: Indian gold, silver prices in fresh setback.</title>
<headline>Indian gold, silver prices in fresh setback.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold and silver prices suffered a fresh setback during early trade on Wednesday with seasonal interest lower than expected, dealers said.</p>
<p>Stockists remained active sellers on reports of a fresh fall in world markets. The markets were closed on Tuesday for the annual kite festival.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) fell in early trade by 100 rupees to 56,800 rupees.  </p>
